  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_ace5e5ee2b86413392b6e0fa49af35c4",
      "statement": "AgentForge's central design thesis is '20% is the model, 80% is the runtime': agent quality depends more on how the runtime manages context, tool use, guardrails, and evaluation than on the chosen model.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L21-L25",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:19c66e8214f87352e903d02093b61434ad7a9f0147663fa6ca0dba6ff5f3c6b6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c764184d46744eac9998f4977c61b93c",
      "statement": "AgentSpec and its sub-models (identity, persona, channel, tools, memory, output, guardrails, eval, deployment, model_policy, workflow) use Pydantic extra=\"forbid\", so unknown fields in agent.yaml are hard validation errors and the spec remains the single source of truth.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/agentforge/core/agent_models.py#L8-L123",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a6ffc55130c9ef9ef391b2dbd84e4f61c867b66be4004fa3c6da40da720f34fc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6b6cf811b2994e72a1a17ad006ced990",
      "statement": "validation.py provides load_yaml_file, validate_agent_spec, validate_framework_spec, validate_orchestrator_spec, and validate_all_specs; the latter walks a project specs/ directory for framework.spec.yaml and orchestrator.spec.yaml.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/agentforge/core/validation.py#L16-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8435bf3f9a8d9eaacce26f03b1a469b26dbf9bc82ba3dc640fa3463720ac1332:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_021c6b558c074ceaa5494d34c6eb333c",
      "statement": "AgentRuntime.from_agent_dir loads agent.yaml, runtime.yaml, and (optionally) tools.yaml from the agent directory; RuntimeConfig is a flat projection with a model_validator(mode=\"before\") that flattens nested model/workflow/memory/output sections and honors AGENTFORGE_PROVIDER and AGENTFORGE_MODEL environment overrides.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/agentforge/runtime/engine.py#L34-L135",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cbf6da5efbc22f37e0de1bbd1d4bf4ab34fde592fec298d4f5706d6b4663870a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5229336f221d4d2b8ef364e7937de24d",
      "statement": "AgentRuntime.run() routes by workflow_mode: respond_or_tool runs the tool-calling cycle, any other mode issues a single provider.generate() without tool schema; both paths are then followed by reflection (if reflection_rounds>0), must_not guardrail check/correction, must-compliance loop, history update/persist, and append to agents/<id>/runs/runs.jsonl.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/agentforge/runtime/engine.py#L935-L1197",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f588fadfd38eef3587c12f45f65ad21ac95c48d2896ae382387a15caed4a2284:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b0b868deb86446eba1d4b8102bb4e3bb",
      "statement": "The tool-calling cycle iterates up to max_tool_cycles rounds (default 3); the loop guard aborts only when the last 5 (tool, args, result) triplets are all identical, so legitimate polling with evolving results survives; a no-tool pushback (up to 2 redirects) and a separate one-shot provider loop_detected redirect exist to pull the model back into action.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/agentforge/runtime/engine.py#L213-L424",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4c3381877bfeced60246e2cfb6ec2256c24346a997602f30c6b532f1c3809845:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3ffe29a733894392a0a58cd9ad013c88",
      "statement": "When max_tool_cycles is exhausted or the loop guard trips, the engine runs a final inference with a completion hint (executed-tool summary plus first three quoted must phrases) that still offers the tool schema, so the model can persist anything it only described; returned tool_calls are executed followed by one closing text pass.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/agentforge/runtime/engine.py#L426-L502",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fe225cd40c7040d0a865b7df6ababf1baffc553fc33bd6ddf93ba92ba220e52a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_12b9e0051a5e43d2ae62d722bda8a14f",
      "statement": "must-compliance runs up to 3 retry rounds: _check_must_compliance mixes deterministic checks (quoted phrase in output or tool evidence, filename-shaped terms checked on disk in AGENT_WORKDIR, rules naming a tool that was actually called) with an LLM judge for open rules, and on failure chains a new tool-calling cycle from the accumulated cycle_messages so previously-read file content stays in context.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/agentforge/runtime/engine.py#L1046-L1146",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:094a04d09bbab20431327bf04e8f42c7ff91133e9fd5118fdad50f3b5f48c4ec:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_65b214d67374423c9a695048d37152e6",
      "statement": "_apply_guardrails checks must_not with the model as judge and, when a write_file tool call produced the deliverable, checks/corrects the file content and re-writes it to disk via write_file, so the on-disk artifact is fixed not just the in-memory text.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/agentforge/runtime/engine.py#L709-L781",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:75fb85c5c541131fff5bfea5af505f36416b73d59d676af031332d37bedaf418:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_107ceed82de4479b94fd3ca020ffd89b",
      "statement": "LLM-judge calls (must-compliance and must_not) use AGENTFORGE_JUDGE_MODEL when set, falling back to model_default, so a candidate model cannot judge its own output and contaminate its verification.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/agentforge/runtime/engine.py#L511-L527",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:69169a457546fe6c60bed84cccfc5f7c5de51aca6a65f5441f6027e843a418ae:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_95e0922cf1b0464ea4ebc75786e86f5b",
      "statement": "BaseProvider is a minimal ABC with generate(ProviderRequest) -> ProviderResponse; ProviderRequest/Response are Pydantic models with extra=\"forbid\" carrying agent_id, input_text, system_prompt, model, history, metadata, tools_schema (OpenAI function format), and normalized tool_calls.",
      "evidence": [
